---
// Core page. Copy authored against briefs/maltipoo-grooming-haircuts.json (2026-07-13).
// Salon prices attributed to live SERP research (Pawpy Kisses Balestier et al., 2026-07-13).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import CaptionedBlock from '../components/CaptionedBlock.astro';
import FactsCard from '../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Maltipoo Haircuts and Grooming in Singapore | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Maltipoo haircut styles (teddy bear, puppy cut, summer cut) and the grooming routine that survives Singapore humidity, with real salon price ranges.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Grooming & Haircuts', url: '/maltipoo-grooming-haircuts' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'How often does a Maltipoo need grooming?',
    a: 'A professional groom every four to six weeks, and brushing at home a few times a week between visits. In Singapore humidity, stretching the salon interval is how coats end up matted and shaved short.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I groom my Maltipoo at home?',
    a: 'Maintenance, yes: brushing, face and eye-corner tidying, nail checks, and baths with a full blow-dry. Full haircuts are worth leaving to a professional; the starter kit includes the grooming set for everything in between.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which haircut is best for Singapore weather?',
    a: 'The puppy cut or a shorter summer cut are the most humidity-proof. The teddy bear cut works fine too if the brushing routine holds; it carries more coat, so it mats faster when neglected.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much does Maltipoo grooming cost in Singapore?',
    a: 'For a toy-sized dog: roughly $50 to $70 for a basic groom (bath, dry, nails, tidy) and $80 to $130 for a full groom with a haircut, with detailed style cuts running up to $200 at boutique salons. Figures from published Singapore salon price lists.',
  },
  {
    q: 'My Maltipoo’s coat is matted. What should I do?',
    a: 'Do not bath a matted coat; water tightens the knots. Book a groomer for professional de-matting, and if the coat is too far gone, take the short restart cut without guilt; it grows back in a few months with the routine reset.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/maltipoo-grooming-haircuts',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltipoo grooming and haircuts',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/maltipoo-grooming-haircuts" schemas={schemas}>
  <section class="container-site pt-4">
    <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12">
      <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Grooming</p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[24ch]">Maltipoo grooming and haircut styles</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[52ch] mb-5">
        The cuts that suit this coat, what Singapore salons actually charge, and the
        between-grooms routine our humidity insists on.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappLink('Hi! Could you share grooming advice for a Maltipoo puppy?')} class="btn-cta">Ask a grooming question</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AnswerCapsule question="What are the best Maltipoo haircuts?">
    The most popular maltipoo haircut styles are the teddy bear cut, the puppy cut and a
    shorter summer cut. In Singapore, plan a professional groom every 4 to 6 weeks ($50 to
    $70 basic, $80 to $130 full for a toy-sized dog) plus brushing a few times a week to
    beat humidity matting.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The three cuts that work here" id="styles">
    <p>
      The teddy bear cut maltipoo owners request most is the crowd favourite: coat trimmed to an even plush
      length with a rounded face, maximum soft-toy effect, and the highest brushing
      commitment of the three. The puppy cut maltipoo owners default to keeps everything
      uniformly short and is the easiest to maintain. Maltipoo summer haircuts go shortest of all, trading fluff for airflow, and earn their name in this weather.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whichever maltipoo cut you pick from the maltipoo grooming styles above, one spec is non-negotiable on the grooming brief: eye corners cut
      fully clear. It is the difference between a stain-free apricot face and a weekly
      battle, as the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-tear-stains">tear-stain guide</a> explains.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The style menu"
      items={[
        'Teddy bear cut: plush + round face, most upkeep',
        'Puppy cut: uniform short, easiest to keep',
        'Summer cut: shortest, most humidity-proof',
        'Every cut: eye corners fully clear',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="What grooming costs in Singapore" id="cost" reverse>
    <p>
      Published salon price lists put a toy-sized dog at roughly $50 to $70 for a basic groom
      (bath, blow-dry, nails, sanitary tidy) and $80 to $130 for a full groom with a haircut;
      detailed scissored styles run $160 to $200 at boutique salons. Pawpy Kisses, a few
      doors down Balestier Road from us, publishes exactly this tier for 1 to 5kg dogs.
    </p>
    <p>
      At 2 to 4kg, a Maltipoo sits permanently in that cheapest weight tier, one of the quiet
      perks of the <a href="/maltipoo-size">toy size</a>. Across a year, expect eight to ten
      salon visits alongside the home routine.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Salon costs (published SG tiers)"
      items={[
        'Basic groom, toy size: $50 to $70',
        'Full groom with cut: $80 to $130',
        'Detail scissor styles: to $200',
        'Cadence: every 4 to 6 weeks',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The between-grooms routine humidity demands" id="routine" tinted>
    <p>
      Singapore is hard mode for a Poodle-cross coat. Moisture keeps the coat damp, damp coat
      knots, and knots become mats within days. The counter-routine: brush to the skin, not
      just the surface, a few times a week; dry the coat completely after baths and rainy
      walks (a half-dried Maltipoo is a hot-spot risk); and wipe the eye corners daily.
    </p>
    <p>
      A note from the shop floor: the once-a-month bath advice in overseas guides meets
      reality here around day nine, when owners tell us the coat smells. Bathe when the dog
      needs it, dry it properly, and nobody suffers; the maltipoo grooming schedule that
      works is the one that responds to the coat in front of you.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The weekly reality"
      items={[
        'Brush to the skin, few times weekly',
        'Full blow-dry after every bath and soaking',
        'Daily 60-second eye-corner wipe',
        'Bathe when needed, not by the calendar',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The first groom, done right" id="first-groom">
    <p>
      Book the first full session only after the vaccination course allows outings, keep it
      short, and let the groomer prioritise a calm experience over a perfect finish. Clipper
      fear is real and hard to undo; a first groom that ends happy buys a lifetime of easy
      salon visits.
    </p>
    <p>
      Between now and then, rehearse at home with the kit's grooming set: touch paws, brush
      briefly, reward, stop. Ten minutes of rehearsal beats an hour of restraint later.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="First-groom brief"
      items={[
        'After the vaccination course completes',
        'Short session, calm beats perfect',
        'Rehearse brushing and paw handling at home',
        'Brief the groomer: teddy face, eyes clear',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />

  <CtaClose
    secondaryHeading="Grooming kit included"
    secondaryText="Every puppy goes home with the 30-item starter kit, grooming set inside."
    secondaryHref="/maltipoo-price-singapore"
    secondaryLabel="See what's included"
  />
</BaseLayout>
